  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-41123-PROJECT-180348</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41123" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">United Nations Industrial Development Organization</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HCFC phase-out management plan (Stage II)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will aim to completely phase out the conumption of HCFCs in Tanzania by 2030, in line with the Montreal Protocol reducuion targets. It was approved at the 87th meeting of the ExCom, in July 2021. First tranche approved for UNIDO is in the amount of US$ 100,000. The second tranche request is sheduled for 2026 and the amount to be requested is US$ 70,000. UNEP is lead implementing agency for this project. Activities under the first rtnache include: Procurement and distribution ODS identifiers and spare parts; development of a business model to set up a refrigerant recovery/re-use infrastructure, conducting a comparative study of performance for various equipment running with alternative refrigerants, train trainers from vocational training institutes on the safe handling of flammable refrigerants and service of HC-based equipment, procure and distribute complementary tools and equipment to set-up one reclaiming centre, and provide tools to regional centres for managing HC; develop and implement a national strategy to promote the containment of refrigerants and the benefits of using alternative substances in their RAC equipment through printing and disseminating publications, as well as airing announcements in mass media, television and radio programmes.</narrative>
  </description>
